# ZL Spectrum Equalizer for WebCLAP

ZLSpectrumEqualizer by ZL Audio (zsliu98), a spectrum equalizer with dynamic bands, ported to WebCLAP. This is not
an official ZL Audio release.

- ZLSpectrumEqualizer: https://github.com/ZL-Audio/ZLSpectrumEqualizer (commit 10388f0, after version 0.1.1)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-zl-spectrum-equalizer.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named
  here.

Changes in this port (`patches/zl-spectrum-equalizer-webclap.patch`): the editor's analyzer and curve loops, which
run on threads upstream, run one pass per repaint on the editor's thread, and the processor builds without its
editor. The sidechain is the bundle's second input. The editor has no presets, no colour schemes, no tooltip
language (English) and no credit tab (a legal notice line in the UI settings instead); the UI settings it saves live
in the page's memory and are gone when it reloads.

